2026-07-08 13:56:00,351 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: To address the client's requirements, we will leverage our Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities to design an AI assistance solution that enhances hospital staff efficiency while improving patient care quality and safety. Our approach will build on past successful deployments, such as the medical-documentation pilot for a regional hospital group.

Firstly, we will utilize our hybrid retrieval approach, combining lexical and semantic search, to provide staff with rapid access to relevant information sources, including care protocols, internal procedures, and regulatory texts. This will simplify their workflow by reducing the time spent searching for necessary information.

To improve efficiency, we will implement template-guided drafting for clinical notes and discharge summaries, allowing staff to quickly generate high-quality documents while ensuring compliance with institutional rules and protocols. Our system will also offer action and verification suggestions based on the context of each patient's dossier, streamlining decision-making processes.

Explainability is crucial in healthcare; thus, our solution will incorporate source citations, retrieved passages, and retrieval traces for every interaction. This transparency, combined with human oversight built into the workflow, aligns with HAS guidance and ensures that AI-driven suggestions are validated by professionals before implementation.

We will fine-tune our model on client-specific material to enhance performance while adhering to defined data use terms agreed upon with the client and our compliance function. Our iterative approach involves corpus selection and curation with client experts, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and an evaluation loop to ensure high-quality outputs.

Performance will be measured using a labelled evaluation set built in collaboration with the client, focusing on metrics such as groundedness, relevance, and factual support. This ensures that our solution meets the required standards of quality and safety.

By embedding our AI assistant into existing clinical and administrative workflows without introducing significant disruptions, we aim to reduce processing and documentation times. Our past deployments have demonstrated the potential for such efficiency gains, and we believe a similar approach can benefit CHRB staff.

Ultimately, our strategy balances performance with explainability and sovereignty, recognizing the trade-offs involved in model selection. By choosing the right model option per engagement, whether it be our sovereign European open-weight model or top-tier proprietary models via API, we can tailor our solution to meet the specific needs of the client while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and internal standards.
